  pearl:'Prophylactic gastropexy strongly recommended for high-risk breeds. Serum lactate >6 mmol/L = high risk of gastric necrosis — prepare owner for guarded prognosis. Do not delay surgery for extended stabilisation. Trocarisation buys time — it is not definitive treatment.',
